// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna — territories (home ranges).
//
// Predators get a territory automatically (radius from body size), so this file only opts IN the
// large HERD HERBIVORES, which otherwise fill every cell to K. radiusChunks is the spacing kept
// between herds — bigger = sparser herds / lower average. Small, gregarious species (hares, raccoon,
// chicken, the snakes) are left OUT on purpose: they overlap freely, as in nature. The overall
// background density between herds is set by TerritoryFloorFraction in the mod config, not here.
//
// These merge onto each species' other overlay settings (lifecycle etc. live in the other files).
{
  "species": {

    // ===================== Vanilla deer =====================
    "game:deer-caribou":   { "territory": { "enabled": true, "radiusChunks": 5 } },
